-- against a pure-digit value misreading as an epoch date); FED_PENALTY_
-- ASSESSED_AMT/STATE_LOCAL_PENALTY_AMT were bare try_to_double() (no guard
-- against the string 'nan' silently parsing as the float NaN). Live-checked
-- 2026-09-20: SETTLEMENT_ENTERED_DATE carries 0 pure-digit / no-separator
-- values across 109,481 filled rows -- no misparse today. The two penalty
-- columns DO hold real fractional dollars live (62 of 4,533 filled
-- FED_PENALTY_ASSESSED_AMT rows, 5,762 of 48,135 filled STATE_LOCAL_PENALTY_AMT
-- rows) -- try_to_double doesn't round like try_to_number does, so those
-- decimals already survive; the fix here is only the 'nan'-string guard, still
-- a landmine, not an active bug. Kept on source() (not ref()): the sibling
-- staging model (models/staging/fed_epa_npdes_npdes_formal_enforcement_actions)
-- leaves SETTLEMENT_ENTERED_DATE as raw text (not every sampled value parsed as
-- a date there), so swapping to ref() would have demoted a currently-working
-- DATE column to TEXT. Wrapped all 3 in place with stg_date/stg_float instead
-- (macros/staging_casts.sql).

with source as (
    select * from {{ source('ripple_raw', 'FED_EPA_NPDES_NPDES_FORMAL_ENFORCEMENT_ACTIONS') }}
